  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "In the courtyard, Mikhail Jekovich discovers that his three-hundred-thousand-ruble racehorse is actually a miniature pony. Meanwhile, Katya asks Denis not to pressure her while her father is in a coma, and Nikita leaves for Saint Petersburg.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Подожди, это же не конь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Зато он очень породистый пони.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Держи коня, мы в расчёте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нас не должны видеть вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Я просто хотел спросить про отца.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Папе нужна операция в Германии.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы сейчас везде ищем деньги.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Денис, пожалуйста, не дави на меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне сейчас правда очень тяжело.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Я сейчас в Питер улетаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но мы так и не поговорили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Стой здесь и сторожи коня.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Подожди, это же не конь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait, this is not a horse.' Mikhail brings out the contrast between 'wait' and 'this' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Зато он очень породистый пони.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'On the other hand, he is a very thoroughbred pony.' Mikhail anchors the line on 'on the other hand', while 'pony' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Держи коня, мы в расчёте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Take the horse, we are even.' The grammar packs 'hold' and 'even' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Katya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нас не должны видеть вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'They must not see us together.' Katya anchors the line on 'us', while 'together' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Я просто хотел спросить про отца.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I just wanted to ask about your father.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'father' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Папе нужна операция в Германии.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Dad needs an operation in Germany.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'to Dad' and finishing on 'Germany'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы сейчас везде ищем деньги.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We are looking for money everywhere right now.' Notice how Russian expresses 'we' and 'money' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Денис, пожалуйста, не дави на меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Denis, please do not pressure me.' The meaning hinges on 'Denis' working together with 'me' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне сейчас правда очень тяжело.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is truly very hard for me right now.' Katya brings out the contrast between 'to me' and 'now' in a few short words. Denis answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Я сейчас в Питер улетаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am flying to Saint Petersburg right now.' Denis anchors the line on 'I', while 'am flying away' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но мы так и не поговорили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But we never actually talked.' The grammar packs 'but' and 'had a talk' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Стой здесь и сторожи коня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Stand here and guard the horse.' The meaning hinges on 'stop' working together with 'horse' in spoken Russian. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
